Archive Contents: CheckDrop, Newcheckdrop2, DropedCar, Readme.DOC, Readme., 
                  Readme..info


This is Version 2a of Checkdrop.. if ya have the first version of this, the
config files will still work, but you will have to reset the list of users who
have dropped carrier already...


I made this program because I was tired of having users drop carrier on my
system because basicly they're too lazy to logoff properly...

For the sake of Speed, the program has broken into 2 sections.. That way, only
the sysops have to load up the whole file.

On this version I have added a few features that will let you check out the
individual users on the list, and delete them Via. the User command at the main
command line.. 

You can make seperate users exempt from being dropped, or whole access groups.

You can also determine how many times an access group may drop carrier on you 
before the system drops carrier on them.

The Status log will keep a record of who dropped carrier on the BBS and who the 
BBS droped carrier on, as well as What port and what Baud rate..

I have also added a feature which will disable the system from dropping carrier
on the users, but will still keep logs of who has done it.

It now also has a feature that will "Forgive" them for dropping carrier on the
system if they're connected at Carrier rates OVER 14.4K  (this does not INCLUDE
14.4K)

I spent alot of time making the Configuration menu as self explainitory as possible
so I won't get into that here.



all you have to do copy CHECKDROP & DROPEDCAR to PFILES:/logoff (or whareever else you
want to put them), create the directory PFILES:Logoff and PFILES:Logoff/Users and 
then add

{#0pfiles:Logoff/checkdrop} in line 62 of BBSTEXT, &
{#0pfiles:Logoff/dropedcar} to line 80

and CheckDrop will do all the rest.

Note: You may want to put CheckDrop somewhare in the Pfiles so that you can 
      access the editor easier.

IMPORTANT: you must configure what access group is considered to have 
           "Maintenance Access" through the (C)onfiguration editor 
           or else all groups will have access to it.

Account #1 will always be exempt and will always have access to the editor.

If you do not specify any accessgroups or users, the default limit for dropped 
carriers is 10

Entering accounts into the "exempt user list" is done with the account numbers
only.

CheckDrop will create 4 different files:
Access - stores your seperate access group configuration
Configdata - stores a list of the exempt user account#'s 
Log - Guess!
users/(UserHandle) - Keeps track of the user.
Disabled - If you have Dropcarrier Disabled
BaudDisabled - If you have the > 14.4K carrier Disabled

Recommended File structure:
Pfiles:Logoff/Checkdrop
Pfiles:logoff/Dropedcar
Pfiles:logoff/Newcheckdrop2       (Manditory)
Pfiles:logoff/users  (Directory)  (Manditory)

